{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Chat, AI streams, logs, and other reverse feeds have a different scrolling contract than a standard top-anchored list. New output usually appears at the end, older history is prepended at the start, and the viewport should only follow new output when the user is already reading the latest item."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Virtual supports this with end anchoring:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const virtualizer = useVirtualizer({\n  count: messages.length,\n  getScrollElement: () => parentRef.current,\n  estimateSize: () => 72,\n  getItemKey: (index) => messages[index]!.id,\n  anchorTo: 'end',\n  followOnAppend: true,\n  scrollEndThreshold: 80,\n  overscan: 6,\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See the full "},{"type":"link","href":"framework/react/examples/chat","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React chat example"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"behaviors","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Behaviors"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"start-at-the-latest-message","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Start at the latest message"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scrollToEnd()"},{"type":"text","value":" once the scroll element is mounted."}]},{"type":"code","value":"React.useLayoutEffect(() => {\n  virtualizer.scrollToEnd()\n}, [virtualizer])","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For server-rendered or restored screens, you can also use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialOffset"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"initialMeasurementsCache"},{"type":"text","value":", but most chat screens start by imperatively scrolling to the latest item after mount."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"keep-older-history-prepends-stable","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep older-history prepends stable"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When the user scrolls near the top, load older messages and prepend them to the array. With "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"anchorTo: 'end'"},{"type":"text","value":", TanStack Virtual captures the visible item before the data changes, finds the same keyed item after the prepend, and adjusts the scroll offset so the message stays in the same visual position."}]},{"type":"code","value":"setMessages((current) => [...olderMessages, ...current])","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Stable keys are required for this to work:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"getItemKey: (index) => messages[index]!.id","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Do not use index keys for chat history. After a prepend, every existing message shifts to a new index, so index keys cannot identify the same message across the update."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"follow-appended-output-only-when-pinned","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Follow appended output only when pinned"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"followOnAppend"},{"type":"text","value":" to keep the viewport pinned to the end when a new message arrives and the user was already at the end."}]},{"type":"code","value":"followOnAppend: true","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the user has scrolled up to read history, appended messages do not pull them away. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scrollEndThreshold"},{"type":"text","value":" controls how close to the end counts as pinned."}]},{"type":"code","value":"scrollEndThreshold: 80","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use a scroll behavior when you want the follow to animate:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"followOnAppend: 'smooth'","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"keep-streaming-output-pinned","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep streaming output pinned"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Streaming chat responses usually grow the last item many times. In end-anchored mode, if the viewport is pinned to the end before the measured size changes, the virtualizer adjusts by the size delta and keeps the bottom stuck to the latest output."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This works with the normal dynamic measurement pattern:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"{virtualizer.getVirtualItems().map((virtualItem) => (\n  <div\n    key={virtualItem.key}\n    ref={virtualizer.measureElement}\n    data-index={virtualItem.index}\n    style={{\n      position: 'absolute',\n      transform: `translateY(${virtualItem.start}px)`,\n      width: '100%',\n    }}\n  >\n    <Message message={messages[virtualItem.index]!} />\n  </div>\n))}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"recommended-pattern","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Recommended Pattern"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use a normal scroll container and normal item order. You do not need "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"flex-direction: column-reverse"},{"type":"text","value":", inverted transforms, or manual "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scrollTop += delta"},{"type":"text","value":" prepend compensation."}]},{"type":"code","value":"<div ref={parentRef} style={{ height: 600, overflow: 'auto' }}>\n  <div\n    style={{\n      height: virtualizer.getTotalSize(),\n      position: 'relative',\n      width: '100%',\n    }}\n  >\n    {virtualizer.getVirtualItems().map((virtualItem) => (\n      <div\n        key={virtualItem.key}\n        ref={virtualizer.measureElement}\n        data-index={virtualItem.index}\n        style={{\n          position: 'absolute',\n          transform: `translateY(${virtualItem.start}px)`,\n          width: '100%',\n        }}\n      >\n        <Message message={messages[virtualItem.index]!} />\n      </div>\n    ))}\n  </div>\n</div>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"production-checklist","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Production Checklist"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use stable message ids with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getItemKey"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Give the scroll element a fixed height and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"overflow: auto"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Call "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"measureElement"},{"type":"text","value":" for dynamic message heights."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"anchorTo: 'end'"},{"type":"text","value":" for prepend stability and streaming bottom growth."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"followOnAppend"},{"type":"text","value":" when new output should follow only from the latest position."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isAtEnd()"},{"type":"text","value":" to show \"Jump to latest\" UI when the user is reading history."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep network loading state outside the virtualizer; prepend or append data normally."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"api-reference","children":[{"type":"text","value":"API Reference"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"api/virtualizer#anchorto","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"anchorTo"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"api/virtualizer#followonappend","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"followOnAppend"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"api/virtualizer#scrollendthreshold","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scrollEndThreshold"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"api/virtualizer#scrolltoend","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"scrollToEnd"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"api/virtualizer#getdistancefromend","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getDistanceFromEnd"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"api/virtualizer#isatend","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isAtEnd"}]}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"behaviors","text":"Behaviors","level":2},{"id":"start-at-the-latest-message","text":"Start at the latest message","level":3},{"id":"keep-older-history-prepends-stable","text":"Keep older-history prepends stable","level":3},{"id":"follow-appended-output-only-when-pinned","text":"Follow appended output only when pinned","level":3},{"id":"keep-streaming-output-pinned","text":"Keep streaming output pinned","level":3},{"id":"recommended-pattern","text":"Recommended Pattern","level":2},{"id":"production-checklist","text":"Production Checklist","level":2},{"id":"api-reference","text":"API Reference","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nChat, AI streams, logs, and other reverse feeds have a different scrolling contract than a standard top-anchored list. New output usually appears at the end, older history is prepended at the start, and the viewport should only follow new output when the user is already reading the latest item.\n\nTanStack Virtual supports this with end anchoring:\n\n```tsx\nconst virtualizer = useVirtualizer({\n  count: messages.length,\n  getScrollElement: () => parentRef.current,\n  estimateSize: () => 72,\n  getItemKey: (index) => messages[index]!.id,\n  anchorTo: 'end',\n  followOnAppend: true,\n  scrollEndThreshold: 80,\n  overscan: 6,\n})\n```\n\nSee the full [React chat example](framework/react/examples/chat).\n\n## Behaviors\n\n### Start at the latest message\n\nUse `scrollToEnd()` once the scroll element is mounted.\n\n```tsx\nReact.useLayoutEffect(() => {\n  virtualizer.scrollToEnd()\n}, [virtualizer])\n```\n\nFor server-rendered or restored screens, you can also use `initialOffset` and `initialMeasurementsCache`, but most chat screens start by imperatively scrolling to the latest item after mount.\n\n### Keep older-history prepends stable\n\nWhen the user scrolls near the top, load older messages and prepend them to the array. With `anchorTo: 'end'`, TanStack Virtual captures the visible item before the data changes, finds the same keyed item after the prepend, and adjusts the scroll offset so the message stays in the same visual position.\n\n```tsx\nsetMessages((current) => [...olderMessages, ...current])\n```\n\nStable keys are required for this to work:\n\n```tsx\ngetItemKey: (index) => messages[index]!.id\n```\n\nDo not use index keys for chat history. After a prepend, every existing message shifts to a new index, so index keys cannot identify the same message across the update.\n\n### Follow appended output only when pinned\n\nSet `followOnAppend` to keep the viewport pinned to the end when a new message arrives and the user was already at the end.\n\n```tsx\nfollowOnAppend: true\n```\n\nIf the user has scrolled up to read history, appended messages do not pull them away. `scrollEndThreshold` controls how close to the end counts as pinned.\n\n```tsx\nscrollEndThreshold: 80\n```\n\nUse a scroll behavior when you want the follow to animate:\n\n```tsx\nfollowOnAppend: 'smooth'\n```\n\n### Keep streaming output pinned\n\nStreaming chat responses usually grow the last item many times. In end-anchored mode, if the viewport is pinned to the end before the measured size changes, the virtualizer adjusts by the size delta and keeps the bottom stuck to the latest output.\n\nThis works with the normal dynamic measurement pattern:\n\n```tsx\n{virtualizer.getVirtualItems().map((virtualItem) => (\n  <div\n    key={virtualItem.key}\n    ref={virtualizer.measureElement}\n    data-index={virtualItem.index}\n    style={{\n      position: 'absolute',\n      transform: `translateY(${virtualItem.start}px)`,\n      width: '100%',\n    }}\n  >\n    <Message message={messages[virtualItem.index]!} />\n  </div>\n))}\n```\n\n## Recommended Pattern\n\nUse a normal scroll container and normal item order. You do not need `flex-direction: column-reverse`, inverted transforms, or manual `scrollTop += delta` prepend compensation.\n\n```tsx\n<div ref={parentRef} style={{ height: 600, overflow: 'auto' }}>\n  <div\n    style={{\n      height: virtualizer.getTotalSize(),\n      position: 'relative',\n      width: '100%',\n    }}\n  >\n    {virtualizer.getVirtualItems().map((virtualItem) => (\n      <div\n        key={virtualItem.key}\n        ref={virtualizer.measureElement}\n        data-index={virtualItem.index}\n        style={{\n          position: 'absolute',\n          transform: `translateY(${virtualItem.start}px)`,\n          width: '100%',\n        }}\n      >\n        <Message message={messages[virtualItem.index]!} />\n      </div>\n    ))}\n  </div>\n</div>\n```\n\n## Production Checklist\n\n- Use stable message ids with `getItemKey`.\n- Give the scroll element a fixed height and `overflow: auto`.\n- Call `measureElement` for dynamic message heights.\n- Use `anchorTo: 'end'` for prepend stability and streaming bottom growth.\n- Use `followOnAppend` when new output should follow only from the latest position.\n- Use `isAtEnd()` to show \"Jump to latest\" UI when the user is reading history.\n- Keep network loading state outside the virtualizer; prepend or append data normally.\n\n## API Reference\n\n- [`anchorTo`](api/virtualizer#anchorto)\n- [`followOnAppend`](api/virtualizer#followonappend)\n- [`scrollEndThreshold`](api/virtualizer#scrollendthreshold)\n- [`scrollToEnd`](api/virtualizer#scrolltoend)\n- [`getDistanceFromEnd`](api/virtualizer#getdistancefromend)\n- [`isAtEnd`](api/virtualizer#isatend)\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: Chat\n---\n\nChat, AI streams, logs, and other reverse feeds have a different scrolling contract than a standard top-anchored list. New output usually appears at the end, older history is prepended at the start, and the viewport should only follow new output when the user is already reading the latest item.\n\nTanStack Virtual supports this with end anchoring:\n\n```tsx\nconst virtualizer = useVirtualizer({\n  count: messages.length,\n  getScrollElement: () => parentRef.current,\n  estimateSize: () => 72,\n  getItemKey: (index) => messages[index]!.id,\n  anchorTo: 'end',\n  followOnAppend: true,\n  scrollEndThreshold: 80,\n  overscan: 6,\n})\n```\n\nSee the full [React chat example](framework/react/examples/chat).\n\n## Behaviors\n\n### Start at the latest message\n\nUse `scrollToEnd()` once the scroll element is mounted.\n\n```tsx\nReact.useLayoutEffect(() => {\n  virtualizer.scrollToEnd()\n}, [virtualizer])\n```\n\nFor server-rendered or restored screens, you can also use `initialOffset` and `initialMeasurementsCache`, but most chat screens start by imperatively scrolling to the latest item after mount.\n\n### Keep older-history prepends stable\n\nWhen the user scrolls near the top, load older messages and prepend them to the array. With `anchorTo: 'end'`, TanStack Virtual captures the visible item before the data changes, finds the same keyed item after the prepend, and adjusts the scroll offset so the message stays in the same visual position.\n\n```tsx\nsetMessages((current) => [...olderMessages, ...current])\n```\n\nStable keys are required for this to work:\n\n```tsx\ngetItemKey: (index) => messages[index]!.id\n```\n\nDo not use index keys for chat history. After a prepend, every existing message shifts to a new index, so index keys cannot identify the same message across the update.\n\n### Follow appended output only when pinned\n\nSet `followOnAppend` to keep the viewport pinned to the end when a new message arrives and the user was already at the end.\n\n```tsx\nfollowOnAppend: true\n```\n\nIf the user has scrolled up to read history, appended messages do not pull them away. `scrollEndThreshold` controls how close to the end counts as pinned.\n\n```tsx\nscrollEndThreshold: 80\n```\n\nUse a scroll behavior when you want the follow to animate:\n\n```tsx\nfollowOnAppend: 'smooth'\n```\n\n### Keep streaming output pinned\n\nStreaming chat responses usually grow the last item many times. In end-anchored mode, if the viewport is pinned to the end before the measured size changes, the virtualizer adjusts by the size delta and keeps the bottom stuck to the latest output.\n\nThis works with the normal dynamic measurement pattern:\n\n```tsx\n{virtualizer.getVirtualItems().map((virtualItem) => (\n  <div\n    key={virtualItem.key}\n    ref={virtualizer.measureElement}\n    data-index={virtualItem.index}\n    style={{\n      position: 'absolute',\n      transform: `translateY(${virtualItem.start}px)`,\n      width: '100%',\n    }}\n  >\n    <Message message={messages[virtualItem.index]!} />\n  </div>\n))}\n```\n\n## Recommended Pattern\n\nUse a normal scroll container and normal item order. You do not need `flex-direction: column-reverse`, inverted transforms, or manual `scrollTop += delta` prepend compensation.\n\n```tsx\n<div ref={parentRef} style={{ height: 600, overflow: 'auto' }}>\n  <div\n    style={{\n      height: virtualizer.getTotalSize(),\n      position: 'relative',\n      width: '100%',\n    }}\n  >\n    {virtualizer.getVirtualItems().map((virtualItem) => (\n      <div\n        key={virtualItem.key}\n        ref={virtualizer.measureElement}\n        data-index={virtualItem.index}\n        style={{\n          position: 'absolute',\n          transform: `translateY(${virtualItem.start}px)`,\n          width: '100%',\n        }}\n      >\n        <Message message={messages[virtualItem.index]!} />\n      </div>\n    ))}\n  </div>\n</div>\n```\n\n## Production Checklist\n\n- Use stable message ids with `getItemKey`.\n- Give the scroll element a fixed height and `overflow: auto`.\n- Call `measureElement` for dynamic message heights.\n- Use `anchorTo: 'end'` for prepend stability and streaming bottom growth.\n- Use `followOnAppend` when new output should follow only from the latest position.\n- Use `isAtEnd()` to show \"Jump to latest\" UI when the user is reading history.\n- Keep network loading state outside the virtualizer; prepend or append data normally.\n\n## API Reference\n\n- [`anchorTo`](api/virtualizer#anchorto)\n- [`followOnAppend`](api/virtualizer#followonappend)\n- [`scrollEndThreshold`](api/virtualizer#scrollendthreshold)\n- [`scrollToEnd`](api/virtualizer#scrolltoend)\n- [`getDistanceFromEnd`](api/virtualizer#getdistancefromend)\n- [`isAtEnd`](api/virtualizer#isatend)\n"}
